  partName: Bolt (2)
  description: The Bolt (2) is a tiny, thin-flat fastener situated at the top-center-front
    of the engine, made of Material.004, and is responsible for holding critical
    engine components in place. Its compact size and strategic location allow for
    efficient engine operation, and its material composition provides the necessary
    strength and durability. Notably, the Bolt (2) is often used in conjunction with
    other bolts to distribute stress and ensure even tightening.
